# Approach
<!-- Describe your approach to solving the problem. -->
we have a dictionary to store the indices in a array by looping through the array   
    We have function make which tries all combinations in the indices and checks if their product id dicvisible by k returning c
if length of indices is 1 we can skip the iteration



# Complexity
- Time complexity:
<!-- Add your time complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
O(N*N) due to make function

- Space complexity:
<!-- Add your space complexity here, e.g. $$O(n)$$ -->
O(N) due to dictionary

# Code
```
class Solution:
    def countPairs(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:
        d={}
        for i,v in enumerate(nums):
            if v in d:
                d[v].append(i)
            else:
                d|={v:[i]}
        s=0
        def make(a,n):
            c=0
            for i in range(n-1):
                for j in range(i+1,n):
                    if a[i]*a[j]%k==0:
                        c+=1
            return c
        for i in d:
            if len(d[i])==1:
                continue
            s+=make(d[i],len(d[i]))
        return s
```

