# Intuition
The only way you can't have a good integer is if you have a card with it on both sides.  You want the minimum, so just sort, giving you the lowest, and check if any card has it on both sides.

# Code
```
class Solution:
    def flipgame(self, fronts: List[int], backs: List[int]) -> int:
        bad = set(i for i,j in zip(fronts, backs) if i==j)
        for i in sorted(set(fronts + backs)):
            if i in bad:
                continue
            return i
        return 0

```

